---
title: Smoked brisket larb
servings: 4
tags: [beef, smoker, weekend]
cuisine: thai
source: Smoked Brisket Larb by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/smoked-brisket-larb
---

> A restaurant recipe: the rub makes far more than one brisket needs, and the brisket feeds far more than the larb uses.

== Toasted rice powder ==

Toast the @jasmine rice{8%tbsp} in a small dry #skillet{} over medium-low heat ~{4%minutes}. Cool, then grind fine in a #mortar and pestle{}. Keep it in a sealed jar.

== Brisket rub ==

Mix the @ground black pepper{1%cup}, @kosher salt{11%tbsp} and @ground white pepper{5%tbsp}.

== Smoked brisket ==

Heat a #smoker{} to 250°F with post oak.

Season the @brisket{1}(about 12 lb, trimmed) with 100 g of the rub and rest it ~{30%minutes}.

Smoke it fat side up ~{10%hours}, spritzing with water now and then. Once the bark has set, wrap it in a foil boat, fat side up, and smoke ~{3%hours} more, until soft and 200°F inside.

Rest ~{30%minutes}. Slice across the grain, then shred.

Warm the shredded brisket with the @beef broth{4%tbsp} in a large #skillet{} over medium heat, then keep it warm on low.

== Larb ==

In a large bowl, toss together @fish sauce{2%tbsp}, @lime juice{2%tbsp}, @Thai chile flakes{2%tsp}, @palm sugar{1%tsp}, 2 tbsp of the toasted rice powder and as much brisket as you like.

Fold in the @shallots{1/2}(thinly sliced), @scallions{1/3}(chopped), @cilantro{1/3%cup}(micro or small leaves), @mint leaves{1/3%cup}(micro or small leaves) and @Thai basil leaves{1/3%cup}(micro or small leaves).

== To serve ==

Pile the larb on a platter and top with chopped @Thai chiles{} and more of the herbs.

Serve with @iceberg lettuce{1%head}(leaves separated) and @cucumbers{2}(sliced).
